    "known_paysim_simulator_artifacts": [
      "isFlaggedFraud triggers on only a tiny subset of actual fraud cases (see flagged_vs_actual_fraud) \u2014 PaySim's isFlaggedFraud is documented as a deliberately weak, simplistic control (a fixed amount threshold), not a competitive fraud signal.",
      "Merchant destination accounts (nameDest starting with 'M') report oldbalanceDest = newbalanceDest = 0 for effectively all such rows \u2014 PaySim does not simulate merchant balances by design (confirmed in Milestone 3).",
      "A large share of origin/destination balance pairs do not satisfy simple arithmetic consistency (newBalance = oldBalance +/- amount), including many rows where both balances are reported as exactly zero \u2014 this is a well-documented PaySim simulator characteristic (Milestone 3 balance_consistency check), not a data-quality defect introduced by this pipeline."
    ],
    "findings_requiring_modeling_to_verify": [
      "Correlations between amount and balance fields (see amount_balance_correlations) are purely descriptive linear associations; whether these fields (or nonlinear combinations of them) are actually predictive of fraud requires a trained model to verify, not EDA alone.",
      "Elevated fraud rates for TRANSFER/CASH_OUT versus other types are a strong candidate signal, but whether transaction type adds predictive value beyond amount/balance features (vs. being redundant with them) requires model evaluation.",
      "Any time-based pattern in fraud_by_day is based on a small number of simulated days and should not be treated as a seasonality finding without further modeling/validation."
